{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-28_ex991pressrelease10-28x26.htm, sha256 7756a9fc1d35dbd6cc615795961c746c9986ec6e5eaf4c8cae6e178751c83b78.\nEX-99.1 2 ex991pressrelease10-28x26.htm EX-99.1\nFOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE Contact: Sam Ullrich (502) 638-3906 Sam.Ullrich@kyderby.com CHURCHILL DOWNS INCORPORATED REPORTS 2026 THIRD QUARTER RESULTS LOUISVILLE, Ky. (October 28, 2026) - Churchill Downs Incorporated (Nasdaq: CHDN) (the \"Company,\" \"CDI,\" \"we\") today reported business results for the quarter ended September 30, 2026. Company Highlights \u25aaThird quarter 2026 financial results, as compared to the prior year quarter: \u2022Record net revenue of $696 million, up $13 million or 2% \u2022Record net income attributable to CDI of $80 million, up $42 million \u2013Excluding 3Q'25 one-time, non-cash impairment and insurance recovery, net income attributable to CDI was up $10 million or 26% \u2022Record Adjusted EBITDA of $264 million, up $2 million or 1% \u2013Excluding 3Q'25 insurance recovery, Adjusted EBITDA was up $6 million or 2% \u25aaWe announced the Thoroughbred Championship Series with the New York Racing Association (\"NYRA\") beginning with the Kentucky Oaks and Kentucky Derby in 2027. \u25aaWe received approval to relocate and expand our Rosie's Collinsville historical racing machines (\"HRM\") venue to 150 HRMs within Henry County, Virginia. \u25aaWe completed the acquisition of 49% of United Tote Company (\"United Tote\") from NYRA and extended NYRA's tote services agreement with United Tote through 2035. \u25aaWe entered into a new $500 million Term Loan B due 2033 (the \"2033 TLB\") and amended and extended our Revolver and Term Loan A facility at favorable rates. \u25aaThe Board of Directors declared a $0.469 per share dividend (+7%) to shareholders of record as of December 4, 2026 and payable on January 5, 2027. \u25aaThe Board of Directors approved a new $750 million share repurchase program. The new authorization includes and is not in addition to the $306 million previously remaining under the prior repurchase program authorization as of the close of trading on October 27, 2026. \u25aaWe ended the third quarter of 2026 with net bank leverage of 3.8x and returned $48 million of capital to our shareholders through share repurchases during the quarter.\nCONSOLIDATED RESULTS\nThird Quarter\n(in millions, except per share data) 2026 2025\nNet revenue $ 696 $ 683\nNet income attributable to CDI $ 80 $ 38\nDiluted EPS attributable to CDI $ 1.15 $ 0.54\nAdjusted EBITDA(a) $ 264 $ 262\n(a) This is a non-GAAP measure. See explanation of non-GAAP measures below.\n1\nSEGMENT RESULTS\nThe summaries below present revenue from external customers and intercompany revenue from each of our reportable segments. All comparisons are against the applicable prior year period unless otherwise noted. Live and Historical Racing\nThird Quarter\n(in millions) 2026 2025\nRevenue $ 315 $ 305\nAdjusted EBITDA 111 116\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Third quarter 2026 revenue increased $10 million due to an $11 million increase from our Kentucky HRM venues and a $1 million increase from Churchill Downs Racetrack, partially offset by a $1 million decrease from our Virginia HRM venues and a $1 million decrease from our New Hampshire venues. The Kentucky HRM increase was due to a $7 million increase from our Southwestern Kentucky venues, a $2 million increase from our Northern Kentucky venues, a $1 million increase from our Western Kentucky venues, and a $1 million increase from our Louisville venues. The Virginia HRM decrease was due to a $6 million net decrease from our Central Virginia venues primarily from increased competition, partially offset by a $4 million net increase from our Northern Virginia venues and a $1 million increase at our Western Virginia venue. The New Hampshire decrease was due to the closure of our temporary Casino Salem venue during the construction of our new Rockingham Grand Casino venue.\nThird quarter 2026 Adjusted EBITDA decreased $5 million due to a $6 million decrease from our Virginia HRM venues, a $4 million decrease due to a one-time business interruption insurance recovery received in the prior year quarter for our Northern Virginia venue, and a $1 million decrease at our New Hampshire venues, partially offset by a $6 million increase from our Kentucky HRM venues. The Virginia HRM decrease was primarily due to a $10 million decrease from our Central Virginia venues that was partially offset by a $3 million increase from our Northern Virginia venue and a $1 million net increase from our Western Virginia and Southern Virginia venues. The decrease from our Central Virginia venues was primarily due to increased competition and a $5 million new tax expense related to live race days under the new racing and HRM tax structure that became effective July 1, 2026. Our Virginia HRM venues continue to benefit from a statewide HRM handle tax reduction that became effective July 1, 2025 as part of this new tax structure. The New Hampshire decrease was due to the closure of our temporary Casino Salem venue during the construction of our Rockingham Grand Casino venue. The Kentucky HRM increase was due to a $3 million increase from our Southwestern Kentucky venues, a $2 million increase from our Northern Kentucky venues, and a $1 million increase from our Louisville venues.\nWagering Services and Solutions\nThird Quarter\n(in millions) 2026 2025\nRevenue $ 126 $ 127\nAdjusted EBITDA 48 46\nThird quarter 2026 revenue decreased $1 million due to a decrease from our sports betting business.\nThird quarter 2026 Adjusted EBITDA increased $2 million primarily due to an increase in our Horse Racing business. 2\nGaming\nThird Quarter\n(in millions) 2026 2025\nRevenue $ 273 $ 266\nAdjusted EBITDA 128 123\nThird quarter 2026 revenue increased $7 million primarily due to increases from our wholly-owned New York, Pennsylvania, and Maine properties.\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "Third quarter 2026 Adjusted EBITDA increased $5 million. Our equity investments increased $3 million from strong performance at Rivers Des Plaines in Illinois and Miami Valley Gaming in Ohio. Our wholly-owned gaming properties increased $2 million primarily from our New York property.\nAll Other\nThird Quarter\n(in millions) 2026 2025\nRevenue $ 2 $ 2\nAdjusted EBITDA (23) (23)\nThird quarter 2026 revenue is consistent with the prior year. All intercompany captive revenue is eliminated in consolidation. Third quarter 2026 Adjusted EBITDA is consistent with the prior year.\nCAPITAL MANAGEMENT\nUnited Tote Acquisition On August 3, 2026, the Company closed on its previously announced acquisition of 49% of United Tote Company from NYRA Content Management Solutions, LLC, a subsidiary of NYRA. Concurrent with this transaction, NYRA has agreed to extend its tote services agreement with United Tote through 2035. Credit Agreement On September 25, 2026, the Company closed the eighth amendment to its senior secured credit facility (the \"Credit Agreement\") to (i) extend the maturity date of its Revolver and Term Loan A from July 2029 to September 2031, (ii) eliminate the 10 basis points credit spread adjustment previously applicable, and (iii) amend certain other provisions of the Credit Agreement. The Company also entered into the $500 million 2033 TLB under its Credit Agreement. The 2033 TLB was issued at 99.875% of the principal amount and has a maturity date of September 25, 2033. The 2033 TLB bears interest at SOFR plus 175 basis points. The Company used a portion of the net proceeds from the 2033 TLB to repay indebtedness outstanding under its 2028 TLB, repay indebtedness outstanding under its 2031 Revolver, to fund related transaction fees and expenses, and for working capital and other general corporate purposes. On October 19, 2026, the Company redeemed the 2027 Senior Notes with borrowings from the 2031 Revolver.\n3\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "Annual Dividend On October 27, 2026, the Company's Board of Directors declared an annual cash dividend on the Company's common stock of $0.469 per outstanding share, a seven percent increase over the prior year. The dividend is payable on January 5, 2027, to shareholders of record as of the close of business on December 4, 2026, with the aggregate cash dividend to be paid to each shareholder rounded to the nearest whole cent. This will be the sixteenth consecutive year that the Company has increased the dividend per share. Share Repurchase Program The Company repurchased 570,169 shares of its common stock at a total cost of $48 million in the third quarter of 2026. We had approximately $382 million of repurchase authority remaining under the July 2025 Stock Repurchase Program as of September 30, 2026. On October 27, 2026, the Company's Board of Directors approved a new common stock repurchase program of up to $750 million (the \"October 2026 Stock Repurchase Program\"). The October 2026 Stock Repurchase Program includes and is not in addition to the $306 million remaining under the July 2025 Stock Repurchase Program as of the close of trading on October 27, 2026.\nNET INCOME ATTRIBUTABLE TO CDI\n"}
{"page": 5, "text": "The Company's third quarter 2026 net income attributable to CDI was $80 million compared to $38 million in the prior year quarter. The following factors impacted the comparability of the Company's third quarter 2026 net income to the prior year quarter: \u2022a $35 million after-tax impairment charge in the prior year quarter related to the impairment of the Chasers' gaming rights. This was offset by: \u2022a $2 million after-tax increase in other charges and recoveries, net. Excluding the items above, third quarter 2026 adjusted net income attributable to CDI increased $9 million primarily due to the following: \u2022a $4 million after-tax increase in equity income from our unconsolidated affiliates; \u2022a $3 million after-tax increase primarily driven by the results of our operations; \u2022a $1 million after-tax decrease in interest expense; and \u2022a $1 million after-tax decrease of the portion of the Company's income from United Tote and our facility in New Hampshire being recognized as income attributable to a noncontrolling interest. Conference Call A conference call regarding this news release is scheduled for Thursday, October 29, 2026 at 9 a.m. ET. Investors and other interested parties may listen to the teleconference by accessing the online, real-time webcast and broadcast of the call at https://ir.churchilldownsincorporated.com/events-presentations, or by registering in advance via teleconference here. Once registration is completed, participants will be provided with a dial-in number containing a personalized conference code to access the call. All participants are encouraged to dial-in 15 minutes prior to the start time. An online replay will be available by noon ET on Thursday, October 29, 2026. A copy of the Company\u2019s news release announcing quarterly results and relevant financial and statistical information about the period will be accessible at www.churchilldownsincorporated.com. 4\n"}
{"page": 6, "text": "Use of Non-GAAP Measures In addition to the results provided in accordance with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles (\"GAAP\"), the Company also uses non-GAAP measures, including adjusted net income, adjusted diluted EPS, EBITDA (earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization), and Adjusted EBITDA. The Company uses non-GAAP measures as key performance measures of the results of operations for purposes of evaluating performance internally. These measures facilitate comparison of operating performance between periods and help investors to better understand the operating results of the Company by excluding certain items that may not be indicative of the Company's core business or operating results. The Company believes the use of these measures enables management and investors to evaluate and compare, from period to period, the Company\u2019s operating performance in a meaningful and consistent manner. The non-GAAP measures are supplemental measures of our performance that are not required by, or presented in accordance with, GAAP, and should not be considered as an alternative to, or more meaningful than, net income or diluted EPS (as determined in accordance with GAAP) as a measure of our operating results. We use Adjusted EBITDA to evaluate segment performance, develop strategy, and allocate resources. We utilize the Adjusted EBITDA metric to provide a more accurate measure of our core operating results and enable management and investors to evaluate and compare from period to period our operating performance in a meaningful and consistent manner. Adjusted EBITDA should not be considered as an alternative to operating income as an indicator of performance, as an alternative to cash flows from operating activities as a measure of liquidity, or as an alternative to any other measure provided in accordance with GAAP. Our calculation of Adjusted EBITDA may be different from the calculation used by other companies and, therefore, comparability may be limited. Adjusted net income and adjusted diluted EPS exclude discontinued operations net income or loss; net income or loss attributable to noncontrolling interests; transaction expense, which includes acquisition and disposition related charges, as well as legal, accounting, and other deal-related expense; pre-opening expense; and certain other gains, charges, recoveries, and expenses. Adjusted EBITDA includes our portion of EBITDA from our equity investments and the portion of EBITDA attributable to noncontrolling interests. Adjusted EBITDA excludes: \u2022Transaction expense, net, which includes: \u25e6Acquisition, disposition, and property sale related charges; and \u25e6Other transaction expense, including legal, accounting, and other deal-related expense; \u2022Stock-based compensation expense; \u2022Rivers Des Plaines' impact on our investments in unconsolidated affiliates from legal reserves and transaction costs; \u2022Asset impairments, net; \u2022Gain on property sales; \u2022Legal reserves; \u2022Pre-opening expense;\n"}
{"page": 7, "text": "and \u2022Other charges, recoveries, and expenses 5\n"}
{"page": 8, "text": "For segment reporting, Adjusted EBITDA includes intercompany revenue and expense totals that are eliminated in the Condensed Consolidated Statements of Comprehensive Income. See the Reconciliation of Net Income to Adjusted EBITDA included herewith for additional information. About Churchill Downs Incorporated Churchill Downs Incorporated (\u201cCDI\u201d) (Nasdaq: CHDN) has created extraordinary entertainment experiences for over 150 years, beginning with the Company\u2019s most iconic and enduring asset, Churchill Downs Racetrack, the home of the Kentucky Derby and premier races of the Thoroughbred Championship Series. Headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky, CDI has expanded through the acquisition, development, and operation of live and historical racing entertainment venues, the growth of the online wagering businesses, and the acquisition, development, and operation of regional casino gaming properties. www.churchilldownsincorporated.com This news release contains various \"forward-looking statements\" within the meaning of the \"safe harbor\" provisions of the Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995. Forward-looking statements are typically identified by the use of terms such as \"anticipate,\" \"believe,\" \"could,\" \"estimate,\" \"expect,\" \"intend,\" \"may,\" \"might,\" \"plan,\" \"predict,\" \"project,\" \"seek,\" \"should,\" \"will,\" \"scheduled,\" and similar words or similar expressions (or negative versions of such words or expressions), although some forward-looking statements are expressed differently. Although we believe that the expectations reflected in such forward-looking statements are reasonable, we can give no assurance that such expectations will prove to be correct. Important factors that could cause actual results to differ materially from expectations include the following: the occurrence of extraordinary events, such as terrorist attacks, public health threats, civil unrest, and inclement weather, including